title: Talks with Other Parties
new-page: true
view-if: {! return !!Q.S && PolishGovernment.outreachAvailable(Q) !}
tags: party_affairs
is-card: true
on-arrival: {!
// Card party.outreach (technical reference 8.1, 17.2; card catalogue 6.1). One talk with one
// partner costs the month's action and no resources; opening and closing the card are free.
PolishGovernment.syncRelations(Q);
for (var id of PolishGovernment.PARTNERS) {
    var status = PolishGovernment.outreachStatus(Q, id);
    Q['pl_out_' + id + '_reason'] = status.reason;
    Q['pl_out_' + id + '_relation'] = Math.round(PolishGovernment.relation(Q.S, id));
    Q['pl_out_' + id + '_gain'] = PolishGovernment.relation(Q.S, id) >= 70 ? 2 : 4;
}
Q.pl_out_kpp_contact_reason = PolishGovernment.kppContactStatus(Q).reason;
!}

= Talks with other parties

PPS has no majority of its own. Regular talks with one party improve our relation with it: +4, or +2 once the relation is 70 or more. A talk costs this month's action but no party resources, and the same party can be approached again after three months. Talks alone create no votes, list agreements or cabinet posts; those are agreed in the parliamentary cards.

- @psl_wyzwolenie
- @psl_piast
- @npr
- @pschd
- @zln
- @jewish_rep
- @other_minorities_rep
- @kpp
- @kpp_contact
- @easy_discard

@psl_wyzwolenie
title: Talk to PSL Wyzwolenie
subtitle: Relation now [+ pl_out_psl_wyzwolenie_relation +]; it improves (+[+ pl_out_psl_wyzwolenie_gain +]).
choose-if: {! return PolishGovernment.outreachStatus(Q, 'psl_wyzwolenie').available !}
unavailable-subtitle: [+ pl_out_psl_wyzwolenie_reason +]
on-arrival: {!
PolishGovernment.outreach(Q, 'psl_wyzwolenie');
!}

PPS and PSL Wyzwolenie compare their programmes for the countryside and the workplace.

